One area where I would like to see greater progress is Screening. While there have been some positive developments, I do not feel we have made as much progress as I would have expected. Hamish has an important role to play in driving this agenda forward and demonstrating stronger ownership of the outcomes. There will always be dependencies on Technology and other teams, but these should not prevent progress or reduce accountability for delivery.

Going forward, I would like to see a clearer and more proactive plan for Screening, including regular model refreshes, deeper analysis to identify opportunities for performance improvement, and a clear assessment of whether a material model change is required. As a VP, I would expect Hamish to take greater ownership of the strategy and roadmap, drive momentum across stakeholders, and ensure that dependencies are actively managed rather than becoming blockers to progress.
